# This worktree is checked out with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to
# CRLF. A shell script that reaches the macOS guest with CRLF fails on its own
# shebang -- `bash: bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` -- and the error names the
# interpreter rather than the line endings, so it reads as a missing shell.
# Pin the guest scripts to LF so a fresh clone produces working files.
*.sh text eol=lf
